    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Ghar Soaps is India's leading natural skincare brand that combines the wisdom of Ayurveda with modern science. Their flagship product- the De-Tan Face Wash- has become a go-to solution for people dealing with sun damage, uneven skin tone, and tanning.",
      "x": 326,
      "y": 1047,
      "w": 789,
      "h": 154,
      "size": "22px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.5px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "What makes Ghar Soaps different? They're completely transparent about what goes into their products. No sulfates, no parabens, no animal testing, and dermatologically tested. Their formulas use powerful natural ingredients like saffron, lactic acid, and Provitamin B5.",
      "x": 326,
      "y": 1201,
      "w": 789,
      "h": 154,
      "size": "22px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.5px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "But here's the thing: when you're selling skincare online, trust is everything. You can't touch the product. You can't smell it. You can't try a sample. All you have are words, images, and claims.",
      "x": 326,
      "y": 1355,
      "w": 789,
      "h": 123,
      "size": "22px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.5px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "That's where the challenge started.",
      "x": 326,
      "y": 1478,
      "w": 789,
      "h": 31,
      "size": "22px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.5px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "h2",
      "text": "The Challenge",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 1604,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 46,
      "size": "38px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75)",
      "ls": "-0.7px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Ghar Soaps had a solid product. Their ingredients were clean, their formulations worked, and they had great influencer partnerships. People who used their products loved them.",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 1666,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 56,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "But their product pages felt... corporate. Clinical. Like a lab report.The Problems:",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 1722,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 112,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "1. Information Overload Without ContextThe product page listed everything: ingredients, benefits, certifications. But it was just text. Bullet points. No human touch. Shoppers had to work hard to understand 'why should I care about saffron?'",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 1834,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 140,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "300",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "2. Missing Social Proof Where It Mattered",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 1974,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 28,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Ghar Soaps had partnered with influencers who genuinely loved and used their products. These influencers created authentic content showing the product in real bathrooms, real routines, real results.",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 2002,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 84,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "But this content lived on Instagram and YouTube. It wasn't on the product page where people were making purchase decisions.3. Tabs That Hid InformationImportant details were buried in tabs. To see 'How to Use,' you had to click. To see 'Ingredients,' another click. To see 'Benefits,' yet another cli",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 2086,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 168,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Each click is friction. Each click gives shoppers a chance to doubt, to leave, to abandon the cart.",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 2254,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 56,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 2310,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 28,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "400",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
      "ls": "-0.3px",
      "align": "start"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "The result? Shoppers left the page without feeling confident enough to buy.",
      "x": 332,
      "y": 2338,
      "w": 777,
      "h": 28,
      "size": "20px",
      "weight": "700",
      "color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)",
